// One-off memory bump for a specific PATHSEQ_SCORE retry, NOT a permanent
// change to conf/base.config's 200GB default (every other sample across the
// 2026-08-19 batch's 10 completed cohorts finished fine at 200GB, several
// using far less -- raising the baseline for everyone would just make every
// future request less schedulable for no benefit).
//
// Built for: unknown_doloromics sample 4A-R, OOM-killed (SLURM state
// OUT_OF_MEMORY, exit 0:125) at 200GB after ~11 min. Its unmapped-read input
// (9.3GB) is >2x the next-largest sample in that same cohort (2A-R, 4.0GB,
// which itself needed to peak at 138GB RSS / 12h26m to complete successfully
// at 200GB). 340GB leaves ~35GB headroom below c-03-04-class nodes' 375GiB
// real memory (`scontrol show node <node>`, checked 2026-08-23) while giving
// real margin above a naive linear extrapolation from 2A-R's usage.
//
// Usage: pass as an extra `-c` config alongside the normal -params-file, on
// the SAME session ID as the failed run so the other 7/8 already-succeeded
// samples cache-hit instantly and only 4A-R actually re-executes under this
// higher ceiling:
//
//   nextflow run pathseq_verify.nf -profile slurm \
//       -params-file assets/config_pathseq_unknown_doloromics.yaml \
//       -c assets/config_pathseq_highmem_override.config \
//       -resume 1e63ae4d-56ea-4424-a3a9-3f8785a20103
//
// If 340GB still isn't enough, that itself is a real signal -- see the
// "Worth flagging as more than just a compute problem" note in
// docs/cohort_registry.md's PathSeq results section before just raising this
// number again.
process {
    withName: 'PATHSEQ_SCORE' {
        memory = '340.GB'
    }
}
